+// SetTrafficLightPosition moves the window buttons of a window made with
+// WindowOptions.TrafficLightPosition, to x and y DIPs from the window's top
+// left corner, as the option does as the window is made, for a title bar
+// whose height follows what the window shows. It does nothing on Linux and
+// Windows, and for a window made without a position.
+func (w *Window) SetTrafficLightPosition(x, y int) {
+	w.do(func(n platform.Window) { n.SetTrafficLightPosition(x, y) })
